==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|baseball|lang=en}} A ball that has been hit with a bat which moves forward by a [[batter]] who is in an arms spread stance, usually in an attempt to bunt the ball past a charging [[infielder]]
#: ''The '''push bunt''' went between the pitcher and the [[first baseman]] who was charging too hard.''
# {{context|baseball|lang=en}} The act of bunting with a bat that moves toward the ball
#: ''The '''push bunt''' is only used in certain situations.''

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[push]] [[bunt]]}}

# {{context|transitive|baseball|lang=en}} to [[bunt]] while moving the bat towards the ball
#: ''Jones '''push bunted''' the pitch.''
# {{context|intransitive|baseball|lang=en}} to [[bunt]] while moving the bat towards the ball
#: ''Smith '''push bunts''' if an infielder charges too aggressively.''